.TH NULL 4 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
null \- null device (data sink)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/null
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B null
device accepts and discards all data written to it.
Reading from
.B /dev/null
always returns end-of-file (read returns 0).
.PP
This device is commonly used to discard unwanted output, for example:
.PP
.nf
    command > /dev/null 2>&1
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dev/null
The null device special file (character device, major 1, minor 3).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zero (4),
.BR full (4),
.BR intro (4)
